**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Before a fit, an experiment's data is flagged when it changed since it was attached or since the last fit run read it (001 §E 'A changed or missing data file is flagged on open and before each fit ("data changed since attach / since the last fit run")'; the S11.2 brief 'Add S4.2's "data changed since attach / since the last fit run" flag'). The since-attach half is S4.2's check (`DataAttachment.statusAgainst`, step 132; `KitProxy.attachmentStatus`, step 134); the since-fit half compares the attachment with the attachments a fit run read, which S11.3's fit runs record. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.2. In `PrefitChecks.fs`, after `prefitCheckWith` (step 369): (1) `DataChangeFlag` = `DataUnchangedFlag` | `ChangedSinceAttachFlag of current : ContentHash` | `ChangedSinceFitFlag of current : ContentHash` | `MissingDataFileFlag`, with `member this.text : string`: `data unchanged`, `data changed since attach`, `data changed since the last fit run` and `data file missing`. It is derived, never stored, so it carries no tag. (2) `type MappedAttachment with member this.changeWith (status : DataAttachmentStatus) (fitted : DataAttachment list) : DataChangeFlag`, over the status S4.2's check answers for this attachment: `AttachedDataMissing` is `MissingDataFileFlag`; `AttachedDataChanged current` is `ChangedSinceAttachFlag current`; `AttachedDataUnchanged` is `ChangedSinceFitFlag` of `this.attachment.contentHash` when `fitted` holds an attachment of the same `path` whose `contentHash` differs, and `DataUnchangedFlag` otherwise. `fitted` is the attachments the study's last fit run read, empty before its first. No other member or option is added. Tests, in `PrefitCheckTests` (step 369), over test-local attachments and hashes: `a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it`: `AttachedDataMissing` answers `MissingDataFileFlag`; `AttachedDataChanged h2` answers `ChangedSinceAttachFlag h2`, also when `fitted` holds the path at another hash; `AttachedDataUnchanged` with `fitted` empty, holding the path at the same hash or holding only other paths answers `DataUnchangedFlag`, and with `fitted` holding the path at another hash `ChangedSinceFitFlag` of the attachment's hash; and the four `text`s are as above.

**Acceptance.** After the flag lands, `MappedAttachment.changeWith` MUST flag a missing file, a change since attach and a change since the last fit run, in that precedence; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a data file is flagged when it went missing, changed since attach, or changed since the last fit run read it`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty s37 invariants MUST pass.
